          "date": "2026-11-26 07:32:56.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-16475 mgc: answer whether a removed OST is set up",
        "message": "LU-16475 mgc: answer whether a removed OST is set up\n\nBefore the MGS lets a new OST take the index of an OST removed by\n\"lctl del_ost\", it needs to know that no mounted client or MDT still\nhas the old OST set up, since a new OSC or OSP with the same name\ncannot be added there while the old one exists.\n\nAdd a glimpse of the config lock, with a new ldlm_gl_config_desc that\nnames an OST index and a new config_lvb for the reply.  The MGC\nanswers it by looking for an OSC or OSP of that OST on the node, for\nthe locks of both the config and the sptlrpc logs, which share one\nlock resource.  Nodes without this reply -ENOSYS, as for any lock\nwithout a glimpse callback.  The desc op names the target type, so\nthat removing an MDT can add its own op later.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I8a7a0ba6edc1e7eca66c986006a960cc3f3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
